          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "**Roster countries:**\n- Yazaki — JPN\n- Sumitomo Electric — JPN\n- Aptiv — USA\n\n**On the duty question:** Yazaki and Sumitomo Electric share a roster country (JPN); Aptiv differs (USA). But I can't actually tell you they'd face the same US import duty — the roster country is a corporate/registration field, not a customs origin. US duty is set by country of origin, which turns on where the harness is manufactured or substantially transformed, not where the supplier is headquartered.\n\n**What the roster country does NOT tell you:**\n- Where the harnesses are physically built. Wire harness assembly is labor-intensive and typically sited away from HQ — a JPN-rostered supplier may well produce in Mexico, the Philippines, Vietnam or Morocco.\n- Whether goods qualify under a trade agreement (e.g. USMCA), which depends on origin rules and regional content, not roster country.\n- Whether Aptiv's USA entry means domestic production — it likely doesn't imply duty-free either.\n\nTo settle the duty question you'd need plant locations and country-of-origin declarations per part number; the roster alone can't do it."
          }
        ],
